Subject: [PATCH] gateway: the compaction writer whose list lacks the model is
 found through routing groups too, and the routing page no longer tells it
 both tried and skipped (#2642)

What changed: both points of yetone's review of 0ab41eba.

The writer left out as its own list no longer lists the model was kept
only by plan's add. A conversation asked through a routing group is
planned by planLevel's keys, which kept its left rows alone, so the
request was refused 400 all the same; and a group in the group planned
by weight passed its sub-plan's left and capped up, not these. keys
records the unlisted beside their rows as add does, and the sub-plan
passes sub.unlisted and sub.unlistedW up with the rest.

And the writer chosen from the unlisted joined the order with its
Unlisted row still in left, so the Routing page told it both tried and
unlisted, skipped: its rows leave left with it.

The tests say the spare, whose list has the model, is never asked, and
that the writer, tried, is not in the routing page's left.

Run at the head this sits on (parent 0ab41eba, itself on ebf3f48f):
- go test -tags nogui -count=1 -p 2 -run 'TestNativeCompaction' ./internal/gateway/: ok.
- go test -tags nogui -count=1 -p 2 -run 'TestCodex|TestCompact|TestCheckpoint' ./internal/gateway/: ok, 19.0s.
- go test -tags nogui -count=1 -p 2 -timeout 45m ./internal/gateway/: ok, 296.5s.
- go vet -tags nogui ./internal/gateway/: clean; gofmt -l internal/gateway/: clean; go build -tags nogui .: ok.

Red and ablation, tests kept, the change lifted:
- fallback.go back to 0ab41eba: the routed-through-group case red again, refused 400 "switched off, removed, or no longer serves", tried none; restored, green.
- native_compaction.go back to 0ab41eba: both cases red saying the writer, tried, is still left out (Unlisted in Left); restored, green.
- the group case was red at 0ab41eba itself before either: 400, tried "".

Not tried: a real ChatGPT account whose plan dropped a model
mid-conversation; the Routing page read through the trace's Left, not
against the GUI itself.

Fixes #2642

